1
00:00:01,105 --> 00:00:01,945
Cheers!

2
00:00:02,025 --> 00:00:03,425
Come on, everyone! Let's drink to Khobfa!

3
00:00:03,505 --> 00:00:04,705
Drink, drink.

4
00:00:04,785 --> 00:00:05,865
Does Rin like you?

5
00:00:05,945 --> 00:00:07,185
I don't know.

6
00:00:07,705 --> 00:00:08,545
What about you?

7
00:00:08,625 --> 00:00:10,025
Do you like Rin?

8
00:00:10,105 --> 00:00:11,425
Remember what I told you?

9
00:00:11,505 --> 00:00:12,545
Whenever you're with me,

10
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:14,625
all the unlucky things that happen
seem so small.

11
00:00:14,705 --> 00:00:16,745
I really mean that.

12
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:41,305
You're awake?

13
00:00:43,105 --> 00:00:43,985
Hey!

14
00:00:49,945 --> 00:00:51,385
Why did you sleep so close to me?

15
00:00:51,465 --> 00:00:53,185
You were the one sprawled all over me.

16
00:00:55,185 --> 00:00:56,425
I should go take a shower.

17
00:00:56,505 --> 00:00:57,345
Wait.

18
00:01:02,745 --> 00:01:04,945
What? Are you going to yell at me again?

19
00:01:05,025 --> 00:01:07,305
Let me shower first.
You can yell at me after that.

20
00:01:07,945 --> 00:01:08,905
Wait.

21
00:01:09,625 --> 00:01:10,865
You passed.

22
00:01:13,625 --> 00:01:14,505
Huh?

23
00:01:15,105 --> 00:01:16,825
I'll let you stay as my roommate.

24
00:01:18,345 --> 00:01:20,425
Huh? Holy shit. Seriously?

25
00:01:22,385 --> 00:01:24,025
Are you in your right mind?

26
00:01:24,105 --> 00:01:26,105
-Yeah.
-You're not hungover, are you?

27
00:01:27,425 --> 00:01:28,585
No.

28
00:01:40,185 --> 00:01:41,785
See? I told you.

29
00:01:41,865 --> 00:01:44,585
I'm the best lucky charm ever, kid.

30
00:01:44,665 --> 00:01:47,945
Stay with me, and you won't have
to worry about all that bad luck.

31
00:01:48,025 --> 00:01:49,585
Okay, Little Khobfa?

32
00:01:49,665 --> 00:01:50,865
I'm going to shower.

33
00:01:52,785 --> 00:01:54,385
I thought you'd yell at me.

34
00:01:56,905 --> 00:01:57,945
What about you?

35
00:01:58,545 --> 00:01:59,505
Do you like Rin?

36
00:02:56,745 --> 00:02:57,945
You're carrying so many things.

37
00:02:58,025 --> 00:03:00,065
I have to stop by the faculty
to hand in my assignment.

38
00:03:00,145 --> 00:03:01,625
I've got so much work.

39
00:03:11,585 --> 00:03:12,985
What about you?

40
00:03:13,065 --> 00:03:13,985
Do you like Rin?

41
00:03:14,065 --> 00:03:15,265
Thanks, dude.

42
00:03:16,505 --> 00:03:17,385
Love, love.

43
00:03:27,585 --> 00:03:29,265
-What's wrong?
-Nothing.

44
00:03:30,065 --> 00:03:32,025
Go. Don't you have to hurry?

45
00:03:32,945 --> 00:03:33,785
Oh, right.

46
00:03:33,865 --> 00:03:36,745
If I don't make it in time,
Prof. James will kill me.

47
00:03:36,825 --> 00:03:37,865
Let's hurry.

48
00:03:38,505 --> 00:03:39,465
Yeah.

49
00:03:41,385 --> 00:03:44,025
You're giving weirdly short answers.
Is something wrong?

50
00:03:44,105 --> 00:03:46,665
Nothing. Just go.

51
00:03:46,745 --> 00:03:47,825
Let's go.

52
00:03:48,945 --> 00:03:50,225
Hurry up!

53
00:03:50,305 --> 00:03:52,385
-Walk faster. Come on.
-Okay.

54
00:03:53,305 --> 00:03:55,985
I feel so relieved
now that I've handed it in.

55
00:03:56,585 --> 00:03:58,465
Thanks for helping me carry everything.

56
00:04:03,265 --> 00:04:04,865
-Is something wrong?
-No.

57
00:04:08,265 --> 00:04:11,905
Well, look who's in a good mood
after handing in his work.

58
00:04:11,985 --> 00:04:13,385
Hi, Khobfa.

59
00:04:13,465 --> 00:04:15,705
Being roommates with my friend
must be exhausting.

60
00:04:20,425 --> 00:04:21,305
Not really.

61
00:04:22,145 --> 00:04:23,025
See?

62
00:04:25,785 --> 00:04:28,705
Damn, it's hot today. I'm thirsty.

63
00:04:28,785 --> 00:04:30,145
Want me to buy you a drink?

64
00:04:30,705 --> 00:04:32,145
Really?

65
00:04:32,225 --> 00:04:33,945
Awesome. I'll have--

66
00:04:34,025 --> 00:04:36,465
A less-sweet matcha latte
with oat milk, right?

67
00:04:42,785 --> 00:04:44,305
You remembered.

68
00:04:44,385 --> 00:04:45,225
Thank you.

69
00:04:58,625 --> 00:05:00,305
He even knows your usual drink.

70
00:05:00,385 --> 00:05:02,745
"A less-sweet matcha latte
with oat milk, right?"

71
00:05:02,825 --> 00:05:05,825
-So what exactly is going on…
-Between you two?

72
00:05:05,905 --> 00:05:08,585
What? What do you mean? Nothing.

73
00:05:08,665 --> 00:05:09,905
-Oh, really?
-Oh, really?

74
00:05:09,985 --> 00:05:11,545
Really?

75
00:05:11,625 --> 00:05:12,825
Really?

76
00:05:12,905 --> 00:05:14,745
What the hell is wrong with you guys?

77
00:05:14,825 --> 00:05:16,025
And there he goes.

78
00:05:16,105 --> 00:05:17,785
All right.

79
00:05:17,865 --> 00:05:23,345
Our activity this semester is
a nature camp outside the province.

80
00:05:23,425 --> 00:05:26,945
This year, we'll be going to Rayong.

81
00:05:31,065 --> 00:05:33,585
Just so you know,
this assignment is worth 20 points.

82
00:05:33,665 --> 00:05:37,545
No absences or leaves will be allowed
without a valid reason. Understood?

83
00:05:37,625 --> 00:05:39,905
-Yes!
-Yes!

84
00:05:39,985 --> 00:05:44,545
Also, each room accommodates two people.

85
00:05:44,625 --> 00:05:46,065
You'll need to pair up

86
00:05:46,145 --> 00:05:48,825
and submit your names to me
as soon as possible. Understood?

87
00:05:48,905 --> 00:05:51,705
-Yes.
-Okay. See you then.

88
00:05:51,785 --> 00:05:52,665
Goodbye.

89
00:05:52,745 --> 00:05:54,625
-Thank you.
-Bye.

90
00:05:56,385 --> 00:05:57,625
Want to sleep with me?

91
00:05:58,705 --> 00:05:59,545
What?

92
00:06:00,425 --> 00:06:04,305
Well, I mean at the camp.
Do you want to share a room with me?

93
00:06:06,945 --> 00:06:10,145
I was planning to tell the professor
I'm not going.

94
00:06:10,905 --> 00:06:11,825
I don't like crowds.

95
00:06:12,905 --> 00:06:14,825
Huh? Hey, Khobfa!

96
00:06:14,905 --> 00:06:16,985
The assignment is worth 20 points.

97
00:06:17,065 --> 00:06:19,065
That's four whole grade levels, Khobfa!

98
00:06:20,545 --> 00:06:21,625
What a bummer.

99
00:06:21,705 --> 00:06:23,385
Khobfa should come.

100
00:06:23,465 --> 00:06:26,785
We were planning to egg him on
to do something to you.

101
00:06:26,865 --> 00:06:29,905
-Do what?
-What? Haven't you heard?

102
00:06:29,985 --> 00:06:32,025
This camp is amazing.

103
00:06:32,105 --> 00:06:36,825
I heard there's even a legend about a tree
that can prove true love.

104
00:06:36,905 --> 00:06:38,105
Yeah, that's right.

105
00:06:38,705 --> 00:06:43,905
Apparently, soulmates
who kiss under that tree

106
00:06:43,985 --> 00:06:45,505
will last.

107
00:06:45,585 --> 00:06:49,225
Some couples who went in previous years
are still together.

108
00:06:49,305 --> 00:06:50,585
Wait.

109
00:06:50,665 --> 00:06:55,105
You guys want me and Khobfa
to kiss under that tree?

110
00:06:55,185 --> 00:06:56,265
-Yes!
-Correct!

111
00:07:02,105 --> 00:07:04,985
You guys are evil!

112
00:07:05,065 --> 00:07:06,825
-Let's go!
-Get back here, assholes!

113
00:07:06,905 --> 00:07:07,865
Go!

114
00:07:18,505 --> 00:07:23,465
A tree that tests true love, huh?

115
00:07:24,505 --> 00:07:25,905
TRUE LOVE TREE: COINCIDENCE OR MIRACLE?

116
00:07:28,225 --> 00:07:30,345
My partner and I had broken up,

117
00:07:30,425 --> 00:07:33,385
but neither of us was sure
we had made the right decision.

118
00:07:33,465 --> 00:07:35,465
So we tried kissing beneath the tree.

119
00:07:35,545 --> 00:07:39,145
In the end, we got back together
and have been together for two years now.

120
00:07:39,225 --> 00:07:41,625
We've been together for two years now.

121
00:07:51,305 --> 00:07:52,705
Hey!

122
00:07:52,785 --> 00:07:54,065
No!

123
00:07:56,105 --> 00:07:57,185
What are you looking at?

124
00:07:58,465 --> 00:07:59,505
Nothing.

125
00:08:01,185 --> 00:08:03,225
What? You looked pretty absorbed in it.

126
00:08:06,625 --> 00:08:08,745
-Krit, Mochi!
-Seriously?

127
00:08:08,825 --> 00:08:12,225
Do you know there's no couple
hotter than you two right now?

128
00:08:12,305 --> 00:08:16,185
Really? I guess Mochi
makes me feel at ease.

129
00:08:35,144 --> 00:08:37,345
Come on. Let me see.

130
00:08:37,985 --> 00:08:39,225
No.

131
00:08:41,745 --> 00:08:43,985
Rin, about the camp…

132
00:08:44,585 --> 00:08:47,545
Yeah, I understand.
You don't like crowded places.

133
00:08:48,145 --> 00:08:50,265
You're an extreme introvert, after all.

134
00:08:51,385 --> 00:08:54,225
Honestly, I don't want to leave you alone,

135
00:08:54,305 --> 00:08:57,825
but if I don't go, I'll lose 20 points,

136
00:08:57,905 --> 00:08:59,505
and my grades will tank.

137
00:08:59,585 --> 00:09:01,105
You understand, right?

138
00:09:03,745 --> 00:09:08,265
But while I'm gone,
you have to be careful, okay?

139
00:09:08,785 --> 00:09:11,985
I'm worried that
without your lucky charm beside you,

140
00:09:12,065 --> 00:09:13,545
you'll get hurt again.

141
00:09:18,345 --> 00:09:20,385
Hey, whose bag is that?

142
00:09:21,425 --> 00:09:22,385
Mine.

143
00:09:23,345 --> 00:09:24,465
Where are you going?

144
00:09:24,545 --> 00:09:26,385
To the camp with you.

145
00:09:27,185 --> 00:09:28,425
Seriously?

146
00:09:30,585 --> 00:09:33,345
Do you still want to share a room with me?

147
00:09:36,345 --> 00:09:37,425
Of course.

148
00:09:38,465 --> 00:09:40,705
I want to keep an eye on you
all the time anyway.

149
00:09:50,945 --> 00:09:52,305
Come on, kiddos.

150
00:09:52,385 --> 00:09:54,785
I think changing your mind
was the right choice.

151
00:09:54,865 --> 00:09:58,225
Trust me. Staying alone in your room
wouldn't be nearly as fun as this.

152
00:09:59,785 --> 00:10:00,945
Yeah.

153
00:10:01,545 --> 00:10:04,145
So why did you change your mind?

154
00:10:05,385 --> 00:10:07,785
Going to camp is basically a vacation.

155
00:10:09,225 --> 00:10:12,025
Besides, I've never been to Rayong.

156
00:10:12,105 --> 00:10:13,265
Aw, man.

157
00:10:13,345 --> 00:10:17,065
I thought you were so attached to me
that you couldn't stand being apart.

158
00:10:21,825 --> 00:10:25,065
You're acting suspicious.
You won't even look me in the eye.

159
00:10:25,145 --> 00:10:28,705
Hey, don't tell me you changed your mind

160
00:10:28,785 --> 00:10:31,745
because you want to prove your true love
under that legendary tree.

161
00:10:31,825 --> 00:10:34,705
Come on! Who is it?
Got your eye on someone?

162
00:10:36,345 --> 00:10:37,825
Nonsense!

163
00:10:37,905 --> 00:10:41,065
Hey! Come on, tell me! Seriously!

164
00:10:41,145 --> 00:10:42,505
Your names, please?

165
00:10:42,585 --> 00:10:44,345
-Khobfa and Rin.
-Okay.

166
00:10:45,185 --> 00:10:46,705
I'll put your bag away for you.

167
00:10:53,985 --> 00:10:55,305
Rin is really stubborn.

168
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:58,825
Khobfa didn't want to come,
but he managed to bring him along.

169
00:10:59,425 --> 00:11:02,385
Maybe this isn't about making you jealous.
Something feels fishy.

170
00:11:02,465 --> 00:11:03,865
I don't think so.

171
00:11:03,945 --> 00:11:05,865
Once Rin finds out, he'll stop.

172
00:11:27,185 --> 00:11:30,945
Shit, I forgot my neck pillow.

173
00:11:31,585 --> 00:11:32,745
Are you okay?

174
00:11:33,985 --> 00:11:36,305
Yeah, I'm fine.

175
00:12:21,105 --> 00:12:23,545
Hey, are you hurt?

176
00:12:32,105 --> 00:12:33,545
What about you? Are you hurt?

177
00:12:36,305 --> 00:12:37,425
No.

178
00:12:38,625 --> 00:12:40,905
Good. Go back to sleep.

179
00:13:02,905 --> 00:13:05,545
Change the song.
I don't want to listen to this anymore.

180
00:13:06,065 --> 00:13:07,465
I want some R&amp;B.

181
00:13:08,745 --> 00:13:09,625
Here.

182
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:11,625
No, this one.

183
00:13:19,705 --> 00:13:21,145
Hey!

184
00:13:53,385 --> 00:13:55,705
-Whoa!
-Stop!

185
00:13:55,785 --> 00:13:57,305
Khobfa, hurry up!

186
00:13:57,865 --> 00:13:59,425
What are you waiting for?

187
00:14:00,545 --> 00:14:01,585
I'm soaked!

188
00:14:02,865 --> 00:14:05,865
Hello to all the teachers
and lovely students.

189
00:14:05,945 --> 00:14:09,825
My name is Note. I'm an officer here
at Rayong Botanical Garden.

190
00:14:09,905 --> 00:14:12,065
-Wow.
-Welcome, everyone.

191
00:14:17,785 --> 00:14:24,505
This area serves as a collection
of biological diversity.

192
00:14:24,585 --> 00:14:27,345
Most domestic plants are from the West,
such as the chamuang tree.

193
00:14:30,225 --> 00:14:33,625
-Why are you guys in such a hurry?
-We've got a report to do!

194
00:14:39,985 --> 00:14:41,745
Have you hiked through a forest like this?

195
00:14:43,265 --> 00:14:44,825
Yeah.

196
00:14:44,905 --> 00:14:47,945
When I was little,
I used to go hiking with my parents.

197
00:14:50,665 --> 00:14:53,145
That's nice. This is my first time.

198
00:14:54,825 --> 00:14:55,945
Really?

199
00:14:59,705 --> 00:15:00,945
Hey, Khobfa.

200
00:15:02,225 --> 00:15:03,465
What?

201
00:15:04,345 --> 00:15:07,385
You'd better stick close to me,
the luckiest guy around,

202
00:15:07,465 --> 00:15:08,945
or you might run into more bad luck.

203
00:15:13,025 --> 00:15:16,585
But you just said you've never
hiked through a forest before.

204
00:15:16,665 --> 00:15:18,185
Can I really trust you?

205
00:15:21,025 --> 00:15:22,305
Of course.

206
00:15:23,105 --> 00:15:24,905
Lucky Rin's got you.

207
00:15:26,505 --> 00:15:27,785
Follow me, kid.

208
00:15:37,185 --> 00:15:39,665
WATCH YOUR STEP, DO NOT ENTER THIS AREA

209
00:15:42,945 --> 00:15:44,385
Wow.

210
00:15:45,265 --> 00:15:46,945
Holy shit, this view is incredible.

211
00:15:51,905 --> 00:15:53,185
Whoa!

212
00:15:53,785 --> 00:15:55,145
Rin.

213
00:15:56,265 --> 00:15:57,425
I'll take this bed.

214
00:15:58,185 --> 00:15:59,185
Really?

215
00:16:00,665 --> 00:16:03,345
Thanks! Now I can lie here
and enjoy the view.

216
00:16:18,345 --> 00:16:19,385
What are you doing?

217
00:16:20,105 --> 00:16:21,745
So we can sleep next to each other.

218
00:16:22,945 --> 00:16:24,825
What if you have a nightmare?

219
00:16:33,025 --> 00:16:34,665
You don't have to go that far.

220
00:16:35,265 --> 00:16:38,105
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

221
00:17:06,305 --> 00:17:08,785
Wow, the view is beautiful.

222
00:17:09,545 --> 00:17:11,665
Yes, Ms. Prae. Thank you.

223
00:17:12,704 --> 00:17:14,704
It's a pleasure to work with you again.

224
00:17:16,065 --> 00:17:17,464
Was that a client?

225
00:17:17,545 --> 00:17:18,905
Yeah.

226
00:17:18,985 --> 00:17:21,825
Engagement was really high,
so she wants to hire us again.

227
00:17:21,905 --> 00:17:24,464
This time, she wants you
to make solo content too.

228
00:17:25,505 --> 00:17:26,585
-Really?
-Yeah.

229
00:17:27,745 --> 00:17:28,665
Hey, Krit!

230
00:17:36,665 --> 00:17:38,105
Thank you so much.

231
00:17:38,705 --> 00:17:42,025
If it weren't for you, I probably
wouldn't have tried anything new.

232
00:17:50,825 --> 00:17:52,625
Oh, sorry.

233
00:17:57,945 --> 00:17:59,785
You're already talented.

234
00:17:59,865 --> 00:18:02,945
Whenever you set your mind to something,
you always pull it off.

235
00:18:03,625 --> 00:18:08,065
No. I could only do it
because you were there to support me.

236
00:18:08,145 --> 00:18:11,145
Come here. I'll give you a reward.

237
00:18:12,585 --> 00:18:14,385
-Don't be a pervert, Krit.
-Hey.

238
00:18:15,025 --> 00:18:17,185
-You've gotten violent lately.
-What?

239
00:18:17,265 --> 00:18:20,425
-So, are you taking Ms. Prae's offer?
-Of course I am!

240
00:18:22,265 --> 00:18:23,585
What?

241
00:18:28,225 --> 00:18:29,105
Rin.

242
00:18:31,385 --> 00:18:34,545
Have you ever heard the legend
of the tree that proves true love?

243
00:18:40,025 --> 00:18:41,785
I think that's a little too direct.

244
00:18:48,345 --> 00:18:49,265
Rin.

245
00:18:51,665 --> 00:18:53,465
There's something I need to tell you.

246
00:18:53,545 --> 00:18:54,505
There you are.

247
00:19:00,545 --> 00:19:03,185
I told you.
If you're going somewhere, tell me.

248
00:19:03,265 --> 00:19:05,025
Don't wander off alone.

249
00:19:20,505 --> 00:19:23,585
You've been acting strange today.
Is there something you want to tell me?

250
00:19:35,545 --> 00:19:36,425
Rin.

251
00:19:38,945 --> 00:19:39,985
I think I--

252
00:19:40,065 --> 00:19:42,185
Shit, can't we just stay friends?

253
00:19:42,265 --> 00:19:43,545
Damn it.

254
00:19:43,625 --> 00:19:46,545
You expect me to act normal? I like you.

255
00:19:46,625 --> 00:19:47,705
I can't do that.

256
00:19:47,785 --> 00:19:50,025
But I don't feel that way about you.

257
00:19:50,625 --> 00:19:53,865
I don't think we can be friends anymore.

258
00:19:57,985 --> 00:20:00,905
Damn, this camp is wild.

259
00:20:01,425 --> 00:20:04,825
Seriously, if you ever fall for someone,

260
00:20:04,905 --> 00:20:07,185
find out how they feel before you confess.

261
00:20:07,265 --> 00:20:09,585
Otherwise, you would
lose a friend for nothing.

262
00:20:09,665 --> 00:20:10,545
Right?

263
00:20:14,185 --> 00:20:15,185
Yeah.

264
00:20:22,385 --> 00:20:23,385
Hey!

265
00:20:23,465 --> 00:20:26,185
